# omega — copy this to `.env` and fill in the key. `.env` is gitignored.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing reads this file but `python/omega/provider.py`, which is the only
# place in omega that knows an LLM exists. A value already exported in your
# shell wins over the one here, because exporting is the more deliberate act.

# Required. Nothing else in omega needs a secret.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Optional — one model for everything.
#OMEGA_MODEL=gpt-4o

# Optional — the two roles, and why there are two. These win over OMEGA_MODEL.
#
# `judge` runs on every event, including every idle tick, and its answer is
# almost always "do nothing". It wants to be small and fast, because you pay
# for it constantly.
#
# `act` runs rarely and does the actual work. It wants to be capable, because
# you pay for it only when something is actually happening.
#
# Leave all three unset to get the defaults shown below. They are commented
# rather than assigned on purpose: a value set here is a value set, and an
# uncommented default would silently outrank the OMEGA_MODEL above it.
#OMEGA_MODEL_JUDGE=gpt-4o-mini
#OMEGA_MODEL_ACT=gpt-4o

# Optional — your phone's location, posted by an iOS Shortcut (see the README,
# "Location from your phone"). Unset, nothing listens at all. The token is the
# Shortcut's password: make it long and random, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`,
# and put it in the Shortcut's `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header. omega
# listens on 127.0.0.1 only; reach it through `tailscale serve`, never funnel.
#OMEGA_LOCATION_TOKEN=
#OMEGA_LOCATION_PORT=7718

# Optional — your inbox, read-only (nothing is marked read, nothing is sent).
# A Gmail app password (myaccount.google.com/apppasswords; needs 2-Step
# Verification), never your account password. The host defaults to Gmail's.
#OMEGA_IMAP_USER=user@example.com
#OMEGA_IMAP_PASSWORD=
#OMEGA_IMAP_HOST=imap.gmail.com

# Optional — more mailboxes beside that one (the "personal" inbox), each
# read-only too. Names are short lowercase words; each needs its own user and
# app password, and its host defaults to Gmail's. A Google Workspace admin may
# have to allow IMAP and app passwords first. One left half-set is skipped
# with one line at startup.
#OMEGA_INBOXES=work
#OMEGA_IMAP_WORK_USER=user@example.com
#OMEGA_IMAP_WORK_PASSWORD=
#OMEGA_IMAP_WORK_HOST=imap.gmail.com

# Optional, on the Mac only — folders a Claude Code session may work in when
# you ask omega to hand work to Claude (DL-104), separated by ':'. Read by the
# relay (`python -m omega --relay ...`); unset, there is no such feature. Each
# folder must already be trusted by Claude Code: run `claude` there once and
# accept the trust prompt. Sessions run in `auto` permission mode, never with
# permissions skipped.
#OMEGA_DELEGATE_DIRS=/Users/you/projects:/Users/you/Documents/notes
